# bench-hooks.patch
#
# STATUS: in use by the waveform benchmark harness; every hook here is exercised
# by real runs. Temporary benchmark hooks, not product changes.
#
# Contains:
#   MIXXX_BENCH_NO_AUDIO=1   - start with no audio output and without the
#     blocking "No Output Devices" dialog, so an unattended run can never make a
#     sound.
#   MIXXX_BENCH_BACKGROUND=1 - move the process to the accessory activation
#     policy: its windows are shown and rendered while it never activates, never
#     enters the Dock and never takes the keyboard focus. Needed for a bare
#     (non-bundled) binary, which Qt would otherwise promote to a foreground
#     application. Combine with QT_MAC_DISABLE_FOREGROUND_APPLICATION_TRANSFORM=1,
#     which stops that promotion - on its own that variable is not enough,
#     because a background-only process cannot put a window on screen at all and
#     renders exactly zero frames.
#   A BENCHFLAG dump of every MIXXX_BENCH_* variable the process started with.
#
# The background hook reports the activation policy it ENDED UP IN, not the
# return value of the call that set it:
#   BENCHHIT MIXXX_BENCH_BACKGROUND=1 policyWas=... policyNow=... applied=...
#            reason=already-accessory|set-by-hook isActive=...
# A process launched from a bundle marked LSUIElement is already accessory, so
# setting the policy again returns NO while the mode is perfectly active; the
# old "accessoryPolicyApplied=false" could not be told apart from a real
# failure. This wording is the one authored in MIX-11 and is kept identical here
# on purpose: one hook, one log format, one parser.
#
# Applies to: clean main 9e670c1120.
